":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788602210778556001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"16f95df4-d783-4f2f-b0e5-a5132ac9d7f4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"47be-ce45-484a-4cc2"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn current `origin/main`, `infra/terraform-github/versions.tf` describes the Terraform provider path as equivalent to the shell fallback. They intentionally differ: `terraform-github/main.tf` locks only `main` so release tags remain available, while `apply-mirror-lock.sh` locks `main` and all tags. The comment hides a security/operations tradeoff.\n\n## Approach\nReplace the parity claim with a concise statement of the intentional tag-protection difference and point to the authoritative implementations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The comment accurately distinguishes main-only Terraform locking from shell main-and-tag locking.\n- [ ] No Terraform value or executable behavior changes.\n- [ ] Terraform format/validate and `make lint` pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/terraform-github/versions.tf","reason":"Correct the fallback-equivalence comment to preserve the intentional tag-protection difference."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["terraform","github","documentation","drift"],"ticket_id":"9eab-ac4b-2c10-4fe1","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Correct terraform-github fallback parity comment for tag protection","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["012d99d7-0ade-44c8-9293-e262889ff70c","2bc93a4c-26ee-4955-9ebf-7c1